WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.470
You, my friend, the first thing you said to me when I sat down was "oh my god"

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:08.580
"You look like somebody I arrested before." Dude I've known you for like two minutes. I don't even know your name

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.440
Can I have all my people who currently or previously have worked in law enforcement against that wall

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:27.900
all the other people, on that side

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:49.770
Apparently people are a lot braver than I am so, you know, or they're a lot more comfortable with their stories

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:53.800
Alright, my disagreers, come on in

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:57.400
I'm just more excited to be here and

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:01.300
To share stories, hear everybody else's story

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:05.720
For me more it's so, uh, in our situations that you're kind of conditioned like

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:07.700
You guys are the enemy, you know?

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:12.779
I don't know how you guys feel about us, or, you know, I've never had a deeper conversation with law enforcement

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:16.559
Probably from your point of view is is that it doesn't always seem like

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:21.689
The justice system is fair. I think that what you find though

00:01:21.689 --> 00:01:23.689
It's if you truly

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:30.119
love this job, and this work that you strive to find that balance in fairness

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:32.200
I'm

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:37.110
Puzzled by what he's saying because I've never heard anything like this before

00:01:37.329 --> 00:01:42.359
Because I mean if it's true what you're saying then how come police aren't policing police

00:01:42.549 --> 00:01:49.289
Why are you standing idly by while your fellow officers are going around shooting and killing unarmed black people

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:51.740
Why is that happening?

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:04.040
I don't know. I probably did.

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:09.320
Sold drugs, that's why I did - I sold a shit ton of drugs and um,

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:16.419
I Didn't have family. I never - you know. I mean I grew up in foster homes. I didn't have any type of family, but I

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:20.619
Fucking knew that when I went to prison. I knew I didn't want to come back to this shit

00:02:20.630 --> 00:02:25.899
You know what I'm saying, so while I was in prison I knew I needed to start there and build a foundation.

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:29.320
I've been out of trouble since 1989 you know so

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:32.820
I chose to commit my own crimes when I was younger.

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:38.120
I wanted the violence. I could have easily chose to do something else

00:02:38.209 --> 00:02:42.009
But I was always there when things were gonna happen

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:47.920
I was talking about - thinking about between my professional life or my personal life.

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:56.800
I think that like you know, it's it's one of those things where like you look at for instance have I

00:02:57.140 --> 00:03:04.959
Have I killed anybody, have I robbed anybody, have I - like all these major felonies now have I sped before? Yeah, absolutely

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:07.660
You know what I hear is uh?

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:12.369
You're telling me there's levels of legality. I mean I used to be

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:17.410
Sort of on that and to - like I grew up well, I went to private schools

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:21.579
I mean, I'm not somebody you know like which stereotype as somebody who gone to prison

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:24.100
You know and then I've gone to prison

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:28.869
And I just find out how fucked up the system is. I mean what about that guy who goes out?

00:03:29.299 --> 00:03:35.949
Has dinner and has a drink. Ends up spending seven or eight years in prison because somebody started a fight with them.

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:38.109
But then I meet people in prison who've

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:44.859
Shot somebody in the back of the head execution style and only got ten years for it you know whereas for me

00:03:44.859 --> 00:03:46.700
I spent 13 years in prison

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:47.750
because

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:53.440
Somebody was hurting my family, and I thought like okay, well we're gonna go get our stuff back from this person and

00:03:53.959 --> 00:03:59.709
I get conspiracy to commit robbery conspiracy to, you know, use a gun which has added another 10 years

00:03:59.709 --> 00:04:05.400
And it's nothing ever happened. You know nobody got hurt and like maybe it's cultural. Maybe it's you know I grew up

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:10.800
Where like you defend your family you know and yeah like was it a bad mistake sure

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:11.760
Can I ask a question though,

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:15.600
like, why your first thought wasn't like, "Let me call the cops to help solve this issue?"

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:19.439
Cause you know, like from my experience growing up

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:26.070
Cops don't help. They just come by, show up, make a great show of doing their jobs and then leave, but I'm just saying

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:32.279
There's no consistency in the system. It makes no sense, it depends on which county you go to which judge

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:34.380
You show up in front of. It's a political game.

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:35.820
It's - that's not justice.

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:37.860
What would you consider justice to be?

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:43.600
I mean, I would like to see that, you know, there would be some consistency if I go to LA County or San Diego or wherever that

00:04:44.020 --> 00:04:50.609
The same crimes that carry the same time, there would be some, you know, consideration for, you know, situation. I don't think there is.

00:04:56.740 --> 00:05:01.320
The criminal justice system truly does help to protect societies

00:05:02.050 --> 00:05:04.950
If we did not have it that there would be chaos.

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:11.580
It may not be perfect right now, but we need the justice system, and we have to believe it

00:05:13.030 --> 00:05:19.169
For some reason it just seems to me that if you're from a wealthier family, you're easy to get off the hook

00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:23.520
When I was fighting my case I had a cellie who was

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:25.810
Fighting the same crime that I committed

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:31.530
For an attempted murder. He had came back said that the judge gave him one year with two strikes

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:35.940
I don't know how that went about but for me, I end up getting ten years with one strike

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:38.900
And his family was wealthy.

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:41.580
In that, did you have priors? Did he have priors?

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:42.660
I had no priors.

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:48.340
I just didn't understand. Why is it that, you know, if your family has more money?

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:51.120
It's easier to get off the hook.

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:55.360
A lot of times I saw that if you have a private attorney,

00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:56.460
high-power attorney

00:05:56.460 --> 00:06:01.739
I guess you have a better chance of getting off than having public defender

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:08.519
That could be a little hole in the criminal justice system, but that's how it is right now

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:10.950
And then I don't know how to address that issue

00:06:11.290 --> 00:06:12.850
so I guess that's

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:17.850
It shouldn't be a game. It shouldn't be a game with people's lives, like how how can I get this?

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:20.940
How can I negotiate a win with this person's life?

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:23.940
At the end of the day man, it's all about money

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:26.280
And it's about numbers, and there's no

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:31.139
There's no money in rehabilitation, man. There's money in recidivism

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:38.700
And if I could give up my job today as a result of no other people going to jail, which means that they would

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:41.300
Actually stop committing crimes I would do it in a heartbeat

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:45.800
Oh, yeah, but there's not too many people like you

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:48.220
If we had a system full of guys like you

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:50.420
That'd be awesome, I think that that's that's but again

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:53.880
See what you just said is that's the perception that you have is that there are no, it's not-

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:58.589
It's a reality for us. For me when I was inside and the nonprofit that I worked for we had

00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:03.870
You know, the programs in there, and this is a class that are is gonna help them

00:07:04.030 --> 00:07:06.839
You know, actually do something with their lives every

00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:12.510
evening while the guys are going to class like, they get harassed and they we come out of the class and

00:07:12.730 --> 00:07:19.589
All the cops are lined up and like, get on the wall, strip-search, tear up textbooks, tear up their personal property, their homework

00:07:19.810 --> 00:07:20.700
like yeah

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:26.640
That's how the system is, like on the way out of prison officers were telling me like, "I'll see you back on the next one,"

00:07:27.220 --> 00:07:29.339
You know, like, that's fucking bullshit

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:42.439
Out of everybody in the circle, that he was the first one to actually voice

00:07:43.889 --> 00:07:50.478
The fact that he made choices. It's in that moment that they claim dominion over themselves

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:52.680
So I appreciate that.

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:53.560
Thank you.

00:07:55.080 --> 00:07:57.340
Don't know how they feel about that.

00:07:58.169 --> 00:08:02.989
I don't think any one of us right here sat here and say like I didn't make my own choices

00:08:02.990 --> 00:08:08.629
I understand I made my own choice. I got myself my own time. I thought yeah, I get the sense that you do too

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:13.759
I think the larger issue is that the system is broken and

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:21.020
that's what I have a problem with. I don't have a problem with taking ownership of my actions, it's

00:08:22.260 --> 00:08:24.400
Society not taking ownership of its own creation.

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:26.060
And I hope you don't hear that

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:28.800
He was the one - he was the only person vocal in saying that

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:34.960
I will ask you this and I'll challenge you. Do you know who your representative is - have you ever contacted their office?

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:35.500
No.

00:08:35.540 --> 00:08:37.700
Have you ever contacted your Congress member?

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:38.200
No.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:39.360
Then I suggest that you should.

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:48.020
and here's the thing, cause you strike me as a very smart individual that has the ability to go in influence.

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:50.940
I agree with you as - I just think that

00:08:51.779 --> 00:08:57.259
You need to take a walk in our shoes. You know, like - and I don't mean any disrespect by this, but

00:08:58.019 --> 00:09:00.889
You sound like a law enforcement pamphlet

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:05.870
You know, like you sound like every perfect thing that they want you to say. It's kind of like when you work in a company

00:09:05.870 --> 00:09:10.099
And the CEO says this is the policy, but when you're on the ground level

00:09:10.100 --> 00:09:13.219
You know that there are certain things that just doesn't work in reality

00:09:13.220 --> 00:09:15.500
I think you have, you know, great views

00:09:15.500 --> 00:09:20.449
And I think you're - if we had, you know, law - like, just a team of law enforcement

00:09:20.449 --> 00:09:24.349
That's exactly like you two, that have the same views, like, it would be great

00:09:24.899 --> 00:09:28.518
You know, but I also think that there is reality

00:09:29.339 --> 00:09:31.339
When you come out of prison,

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:34.699
Everything is just so stacked against you, like it seems that that's that commonality

00:09:34.890 --> 00:09:37.369
So like when a friend - since when I talked about coming out of military

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:42.380
I had people that told me when and where to be, all these rules and regulations, and when I got out

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:46.100
You know, there was nobody there. Same thing happens in prison.

00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:49.740
You have to break out of the prison mind mentality.

00:09:49.780 --> 00:09:52.460
Here's the difference between

00:09:52.460 --> 00:09:55.160
The mil- and I agree with you, there's a lot of similarities,

00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:58.819
There are a lot of commonalities with prison in the military, however when you're in the military

00:09:59.579 --> 00:10:03.859
You're told you're the men of this country, are the defenders of this country. You're men.

00:10:04.440 --> 00:10:06.000
When you go to prison,

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:08.209
We were told that we're pieces of shit,

00:10:08.209 --> 00:10:14.959
We were told that we're animals, you know, and when you've gone through a decade of that, it - it gets in your head,

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:19.420
Inside your mind. It's like, "who am I," like, "who am I to think that I can do these things?"

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:21.580
it just

00:10:22.320 --> 00:10:26.380
Turns you into nothing, you know, and it makes you believe that you're nothing, that you can't do it

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:32.539
And that's something that you can't put into, you know, LAPD policy, you know, and that's what

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:36.100
the justice system does to you, like it breaks you.

00:10:36.100 --> 00:10:38.100
But you know what, I can tell you this

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:39.949
Me looking at you,

00:10:39.949 --> 00:10:46.580
I don't see any of the things that you talk about. I would hope for you, for actually all three of you,

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:51.200
that you know that you guys are able to escape those

00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:55.320
Boundaries that have been created, because guess what, at the end of the day,

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:59.299
Like, you have one life to live and it's going to be predicated upon the decisions that you make now.

00:11:10.260 --> 00:11:12.260
I honestly believe that

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:16.480
They have a structure in place

00:11:17.340 --> 00:11:18.480
that

00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:20.120
can help.

00:11:20.120 --> 00:11:25.760
The people who are running it are the ones that need adjusting

00:11:26.840 --> 00:11:32.760
I think it needs a lot of work. I think the resources are put in to a lot of the wrong

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:35.629
places and I'm not okay with

00:11:36.150 --> 00:11:37.400
Saying "well

00:11:37.400 --> 00:11:41.780
this is what we got so let's try to work with it,"  like, no I think that there should be moves

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:45.320
To try to improve the system, like I don't think we should ever be content.

00:11:45.320 --> 00:11:52.620
You know, like I said unfortunately when the budget crisis happens, training is the first one that goes out the door

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:58.580
I think they need more training. If they're training to save the one life, I think it is worth it.

00:11:58.580 --> 00:12:00.700
I also think communication,

00:12:00.700 --> 00:12:04.840
to build a unity in a community. That way that it can

00:12:05.340 --> 00:12:12.800
be trusted with one another and be able to work with one another with all the challenges that's going on in this chaotic world

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:25.640
do you have any information on your non profit organization?

00:12:25.660 --> 00:12:29.380
I do actually. Let me give you - you can look us up.

00:12:32.060 --> 00:12:34.180
Hey guys much appreciation

00:12:34.490 --> 00:12:37.060
We get to do what we love because you all watch our videos

00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:40.239
So if you really love us, you'll continue to keep watching videos.

00:12:40.240 --> 00:12:43.210
There's more right here that you can check out, you probably haven't seen all of them

00:12:43.210 --> 00:12:47.919
And if you really want to just commit to us you can subscribe right here. I'll be around,

00:12:47.920 --> 00:12:50.800
I'll be at the end of some more videos, and I will keep in touch. Peace.

